inline.body:
`extraMeta.contains` stores the raw subschema, and `toJSONSchema` flat-merges metadata without rewriting nested `$ref`s or extracting `$defs` for them, so a `contains` that points into `$defs` re-emits a reference the output document never defines:

```ts
z.toJSONSchema(z.fromJSONSchema({
  type: "array",
  contains: { $ref: "#/$defs/Foo" },
  $defs: { Foo: { type: "object", properties: { id: { type: "string" } }, required: ["id"] } },
}));
// { type: "array", items: {}, contains: { $ref: "#/$defs/Foo" } }  — no $defs anywhere
```

Enforcement itself is correct here; only the round-tripped document is invalid. The pre-existing `propertyNames` carry reproduces this identically, so it isn't introduced by this PR — but `propertyNames` constrains key strings and is almost never a `$ref`, whereas `contains` is a full item schema where a `$ref` is the normal way to write it. Fine to leave for the `@zod/json` work if you'd rather not grow the carry here; flagging it so the choice is deliberate.

